## 5. Access Control

### S3 Bucket Policies

#### Website Bucket (Público via CloudFront)
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "cloudfront.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::portfolio-website/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "AWS:SourceArn": "arn:aws:cloudfront::ACCOUNT:distribution/DIST_ID"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Assets Bucket (Privado)
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::portfolio-assets"],
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "false"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

### Public Access Block

```
Website Bucket:
├── Block Public Acls: FALSE (permite CloudFront)
├── Ignore Public Acls: FALSE
├── Block Public Policy: FALSE
└── Restrict Public Buckets: FALSE

Assets Bucket:
├── Block Public Acls: TRUE ✓
├── Ignore Public Acls: TRUE ✓
├── Block Public Policy: TRUE ✓
└── Restrict Public Buckets: TRUE ✓
```

